            <ArticleTitle>Does a bloody tap prevent postdural puncture headache?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>628-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The regional anaesthesia records of 274 obstetric patients who had inadvertent dural puncture were reviewed to see whether a bloody dural tap resulted in a lower incidence of postdural puncture headache. No such influence was found.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
